  "lyrics": {
    "rawText": "\nI measure truth in decimal dust  \nRounding off the edges of trust  \nError bars around each claim  \nConfidence without a name  \n\nEvery promise quantified  \nStandard deviance inside  \n\nMargin of error, wide as a lie  \nSignal is clean but the data will cry  \nTrust is a theorem we try to defend  \nProof in the middle that breaks at the end  \n\nFeedback loops in hidden code  \nBias on a heavy load  \nRandom noise across the wire  \nTruth compressed in sampled fire  \n\nIf I flip the coin enough  \nHeads feels honest, tails feels rough  \nYet both obey the silent law  \nChance and pattern interlock  \n\n\nMargin of error, drawn in red  \nFacts we trust and lies we spread  \nBetween the doubt and what we know  \nDeterministic undertow  \n\nMargin of error"
  },
